{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-29", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curves (Pull 1, Standard, Push 1-3) and spectral sensitivity digitised from the Agfa Professional Films technical data sheet F-PF-E3/E4 (page 9, Agfa Scala 200x). Original data are property of Agfa-Gevaert / AgfaPhoto. Family axis holds the exposure index (EI) 100/200/400/800/1600 (Pull 1 ... Push 3); each curve is shifted so that log E = 0 gives net density 0.85 (mid-grey). Derived from spektrafilm profile format; modified by graineo.", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; only the profile format and wavelength grid taken from spektrafilm."}, "info": {"stock": "agfa_scala_200x", "name": "Agfa Scala 200x Black and White Reversal Film", "type": "positive", "support": "film", "stage": "filming", "use": "still", "antihalation": "strong", "target_print": null, "channel_model": "bw", "densitometer": "diffuse_visual", "log_sensitivity_density_over_min": 1.0, "reference_illuminant": "D55", "viewing_illuminant": "D50", "default_look": {"film_dev": 200.0, "grain": 1.0, "print_ev": -0.2, "taking_filter": "rot25", "taking_filter_amount": 0.2}, "card": {"maker": "Agfa", "iso": 200, "type": "Schwarzwei\u00df-Umkehrfilm (Dia, direkt positiv)", "rms": 11, "additional": "120 lp/mm (Kontrast 1000:1)", "text": "Der Schwarzwei\u00df-Diafilm: sehr hohe Dichte (Dmax bis 3,1), steile Kontraste und klare, harte Tonwerte, wie man sie von Schwarzwei\u00df-Dias kennt. Mit Push (EI 400 bis 1600) wird er noch kontrastreicher und verliert Schw\u00e4rze. Kein Papier, das Bild entsteht direkt auf dem Film.", "source": "Agfa Scala 200x", "process": "Scala-Prozess (spezielle Schwarzwei\u00df-Umkehrentwicklung)", "suitable": ["Schwarzwei\u00df-Dia-Look", "Portr\u00e4t mit hartem Licht", "Architektur und Grafik"], "less_suitable": ["weiche Hautt\u00f6ne", "flache Motive ohne Kontrast"], "tips": ["Entwicklung: 100 (Pull), 200 (Standard), 400, 800, 1600 (Push). Je h\u00f6her, desto h\u00e4rter und k\u00f6rniger, bei sinkendem Dmax; die Filmlooks \u201eScala \u00b7 klar hart\u201c (EI 400) und \u201eScala \u00b7 verblasst hart\u201c (mit Papier matt) zeigen das.", "Aufnahmefilter Gr\u00fcn (11) liegt im Look \u201eAbgestimmt\u201c bei etwa 35 %: Haut bleibt hell, Laub nicht zu hell."], "facts": [{"text": "Das Datenblatt nennt den Scala-Prozess als speziellen Prozess, der nur in autorisierten Scala-Laboren lief. Mit Push-Entwicklung steigen Empfindlichkeit und Kontrast (EI 400, 800, 1600), Dmax sinkt und das Korn wird gr\u00f6ber; Pull (EI 100) macht ihn flacher und feiner.", "source": "Agfa Technical Data F-PF-E4 (Juli 2003)"}]}, "grain_size_classes": {"classes": 4, "area_spread": 5.0, "speed_exponent": 1.0}}, "data": {"wavelengths": [380.0, 385.0, 390.0, 395.0, 400.0, 405.0, 410.0, 415.0, 420.0, 425.0, 430.0, 435.0, 440.0, 445.0, 450.0, 455.0, 460.0, 465.0, 470.0, 475.0, 480.0, 485.0, 490.0, 495.0, 500.0, 505.0, 510.0, 515.0, 520.0, 525.0, 530.0, 535.0, 540.0, 545.0, 550.0, 555.0, 560.0, 565.0, 570.0, 575.0, 580.0, 585.0, 590.0, 595.0, 600.0, 605.0, 610.0, 615.0, 620.0, 625.0, 630.0, 635.0, 640.0, 645.0, 650.0, 655.0, 660.0, 665.0, 670.0, 675.0, 680.0, 685.0, 690.0, 695.0, 700.0, 705.0, 710.0, 715.0, 720.0, 725.0, 730.0, 735.0, 740.